package com.simon.dailyrhythm;
import android.app.Activity;
import android.os.Bundle;
import android.widget.*;

public class PrivacyActivity extends Activity {
    @Override public void onCreate(Bundle b) {
        super.onCreate(b);
        ScrollView scroll = new ScrollView(this);
        TextView text = new TextView(this);
        text.setPadding(32, 64, 32, 48); text.setTextSize(18);
        text.setText("Daily Rhythm — Privacy\n\nMeals, bowel logs, water, caffeine, vape sessions, orgasm events, mood ratings, recipes and saved AI reviews stay in this app's private storage on your phone. Android cloud backup is disabled. There is no advertising or analytics. Network access is used only for the optional automatic nutrition connection.\n\nOptional Health Connect permissions let you read steps, distance, sleep, heart rate, resting heart rate, weight, active and total burned calories, hydration and nutrition. Readings are shown on screen and can be read for a 14- or 28-day review. While the app is open, permitted source records in the available 28-day window are archived privately once a day for backup. Per-category status reports gaps. The app never writes those records back. You can grant only the categories you want and revoke them in Health Connect settings.\n\nGarmin and Google apps must separately share their data with Health Connect. This app cannot access private Garmin metrics that those apps do not share. The desktop USB helper can copy watch FIT files to a private local cache, decode documented stress and other samples with Garmin’s FIT SDK, and import selected readings into private phone storage. Raw files may contain sensitive health/location data and remain on your computer. Imported snapshots are separate from the journal backup. Direct Garmin cloud API access and Body Battery are not configured. No manual Garmin entry is required.\n\nAI help uses your separate ChatGPT app or browser. Review prompts include selected health, imported Garmin FIT and journal summaries and may include caffeine, vape, orgasm and mood event details if you choose. Private notes are excluded. Meal ingredient descriptions are included for weekly nutrition estimates. Weekly health review is manual: copying a prompt places it on the device clipboard, and ChatGPT receives it only when you paste and send it there. Its data policies then apply. Optional automatic nutrition uses your own OpenAI API key, encrypted with Android Keystore and excluded from backups. When enabled, food descriptions, ingredients and portions are sent to OpenAI after saving, with store=false and a local maximum of 300 attempts per month. Private notes and full health history are not sent through this connection. Pause or remove the key in AI help. API charges use your API account, and the provider’s data policies apply. Nutrition answers are estimates and can be wrong. Saved reviews remain in private app storage.\n\nThe computer helper makes dated, verified backups of app files, captured Health Connect records and cached Garmin FIT files. Cloud backup uses only the folder you choose; sharing permissions affect who can read it. JSON and CSV journal exports include sensitive information. Export only to a destination you trust. Imported backups replace the current local journal after confirmation. Deleting the journal does not delete records in Health Connect. Uninstalling removes the journal; export a backup first if you want to keep it.\n\nThe optional 8 p.m. reminder displays a discreet notification on this device. Exact timing requires Android's alarms permission.\n\nThis is a personal tracking tool, not a diagnostic service.\n\nVersion 0.6.0 • October 2026");
        scroll.addView(text); setContentView(scroll);
    }
}
